<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17803" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fātus</span></b> , ūs,
			m.
		for. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A word</i>, <i>saying</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 7, §
			802</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Esp., <i>an oracle</i>, <i>a
			prophecy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Deliaco fatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ficta fatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 13</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Apollinis fatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Fate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incerto fatu fortunae aliorsum prorupit
					eventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 5, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Petr. 42, 77 al.</span></i>; v. fatum,
			II. A.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
